#
# Conformance case: paraconsistency/within-world-glut
# AC: paraconsistency — a WITHIN-world contradiction emits a captured witness (the
# right-hand half of the Paraconsistency corpus invariant; design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md
# §"A within-world contradiction emits witnesses", and §"The coherence certificate"
# §"Undisclosed contradiction, defined").
#
# This is the behavioral counterpart to paraconsistency/cross-world-isolation, which
# proves the LEFT half (a contradiction split across two worlds stays isolated and
# each world is `consistent`). Here the SAME contradictory pair is confined to a
# SINGLE world `w`, so the glut is genuinely within-world and the native DL
# consistency path (gmeow_logic::reason::dl_consistency, folding from the same closure
# as reason_all) populates an owl:Nothing clash for `w`. The harness diffs the
# per-world verdict against expected/verdicts.json: the world is `inconsistent`,
# i.e. the within-world glut was CAPTURED and SURFACED as a contradiction witness
# rather than silently swallowed or exploded across the bundle.
#
# verdict_mode=consistency: the OWL EDB is the world-scoped N-Quads in input.nq,
# decided by the native DL path; this file exists only to satisfy the per-case
# anatomy and is NOT compiled in consistency mode.
#
# Graph-isolation note (LOGIC-CONFORMANCE §"Tests as ontology data"): this
# contradiction fixture lives in the conformance corpus, which is OUTSIDE the
# production owl:imports closure by construction — it can never make the production
# ontology appear inconsistent. Disclosure here is "capture + surfacing": the witness
# IS captured (the world is reported `inconsistent`), so the contradiction is
# disclosed, not undisclosed.
#
# What this case GENUINELY checks (harness-observable): the reasoning verdict — a
# within-world glut yields a captured, surfaced contradiction witness (`inconsistent`).
# What it does NOT and CANNOT check here: the permitted-vs-forbidden CLASSIFICATION of
# that disclosed glut (coherent under a glut-admitting contract vs a forbidden integrity
# violation under a glut-forbidding contract). That classification is computed in Rust
# off the ReasoningResult by the contract's ContradictionPolicy
# (crates/logic/src/certificate.rs::CoherenceOutcome::from_reasoning_result) and is NOT
# folded into the reasoned/materialized graph; the conformance profile surface is closed
# and carries no admissible_valuation facet, so the harness cannot evaluate it as
# ontology data. It is pinned by the Rust certificate tests
# (permitted_glut_is_coherent / forbidden_glut_refuses_and_issues_no_certificate).
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
